# Review router (base)

Use the most specific applicable **review rule** for the task. Apply additional review rules in the same context when a task spans risk areas (e.g. model change + incremental safety + reporting impact).

Pause vs implement: [safe-change-review](safe-change-review.mdc#plan-before-edit) only — do not duplicate that gate here.

Review-style answers: [agent-output-contract](agent-output-contract.mdc).

**Rules vs subagents:** files under `.cursor/rules` instruct the current session. They are not independent reviewers. Reserve “agent” / subagent for `.cursor/agents` (and skills those agents load). Launch a subagent only when the repo overlay says so (high-risk incremental, shared macros, identity, multi-mart reporting, unclear data defects, final PR review if a subagent exists).

When the repo overlay requires a verification skill, run it before claiming a dbt change is complete.

**Domain and repo routing:** see the repo router overlay (e.g. `pew-dbt-router-overlay.mdc` in dbt repos).
